WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.633
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:04.222
- [Narrator] We came together
to accomplish a mission.

00:00:04.222 --> 00:00:07.782
We will be walking around
six to eight hours.

00:00:07.782 --> 00:00:09.555
We want to show the world

00:00:09.555 --> 00:00:11.551
that with the proper prosthetic care,

00:00:11.551 --> 00:00:13.917
and orthotic care, it
makes a big difference

00:00:13.917 --> 00:00:15.417
in someone's life.

00:00:19.492 --> 00:00:20.913
(gentle music)
(clicking)

00:00:20.913 --> 00:00:22.688
(rustling)

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.450
My name's Kionte Storey.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.617
I lost my leg back in 2010

00:00:28.173 --> 00:00:30.155
overseas in Afghanistan.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:33.095
I'm with the United States Marines.

00:00:33.095 --> 00:00:36.751
After my injury, I felt lost and confused.

00:00:36.751 --> 00:00:39.701
A lot of questions of
why, why am I still alive?

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:40.942
Why am I here?

00:00:40.942 --> 00:00:43.682
Suicidal thoughts, which
made waking up everyday

00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:44.805
very difficult.

00:00:44.805 --> 00:00:46.216
(cheering)

00:00:46.216 --> 00:00:49.656
Being active for me
just became my therapy.

00:00:49.656 --> 00:00:52.183
I found myself inspiring others,

00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:54.935
and motivating others
to be active as well.

00:00:54.935 --> 00:00:57.518
(gentle music)

00:00:58.673 --> 00:01:00.696
Currently we're in Ecuador climbing

00:01:00.696 --> 00:01:03.010
for Range of Motion Project,

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.885
which is a local organization
providing prosthetic

00:01:05.885 --> 00:01:08.509
and orthotic care to countries

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:11.523
who don't have the means
to provide such care

00:01:11.523 --> 00:01:13.023
to their citizens.

00:01:14.608 --> 00:01:19.517
We have 10 to 12 amputees
climbing Cayambe Volcano.

00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:21.281
We all come from different backgrounds

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.182
and all different injuries.

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:26.175
To be a part of such a team,

00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:29.558
to me is very, very important,
and it's very inspiring.

00:01:29.558 --> 00:01:31.427
(gentle music)

00:01:31.427 --> 00:01:32.866
Summiting Cayambe from the refuge

00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:34.509
will take about 12 hours.

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:36.359
We have the equipment and the gear,

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:38.275
but we have to be patient and
wait for the right weather

00:01:38.275 --> 00:01:40.897
to get to the summit safely.

00:01:40.897 --> 00:01:43.316
Whether we summit Cayambe Volcano or not,

00:01:43.316 --> 00:01:46.197
it is just a small part
of what we're here to do.

00:01:46.197 --> 00:01:48.821
With this climb, I hope
others will learn a lot

00:01:48.821 --> 00:01:52.512
about themselves and their abilities.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.382
They can do anything they want to.

00:01:54.382 --> 00:01:57.465
There is nothing that is impossible.

